<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net"><diagram id="p_01_csi_vs_rssi" name="01-csi-vs-rssi"><mxGraphModel dx="800" dy="600" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1280" pageHeight="840" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="0" /><mxCell id="1" parent="0" /><mxCell id="title" value="CSI keeps the per-subcarrier fingerprint that RSSI averages away - and a moving body changes only the dynamic paths" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=16;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#ffffff;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="12" width="1240" height="34" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="room" value="A room, seen from above (schematic, not to scale) [A1]" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fbfbfb;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="62" width="620" height="440" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="wall" value="wall / furniture = STATIC reflector" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#eeeeee;strokeColor=#666666;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="120" y="96" width="420" height="16" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="tx" value="Transmitter (AP)&#10;sends known&#10;training symbols" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="50" y="250" width="120" height="62" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="rx" value="Receiver (device)&#10;estimates H per&#10;subcarrier" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="500" y="250" width="130" height="62" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="person" value="person&#10;moves" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="300" y="395" width="56" height="80" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="los_lbl" value="line of sight (static)" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#fbfbfb;strokeColor=#fbfbfb;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="250" y="258" width="150" height="20" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="wall_lbl" value="reflected path&#10;(static)" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#fbfbfb;strokeColor=#fbfbfb;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="458" y="126" width="150" height="34" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="dyn_lbl" value="reflected path&#10;(DYNAMIC: its length&#10;changes as she moves)" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#fbfbfb;strokeColor=#fbfbfb;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#b85450;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="420" y="440" width="150" height="48" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="model" value="The channel at subcarrier frequency f is the sum of all paths [A1; Ma et al. 2019]:&#10;      H(f) = Σᵢ aᵢ · exp(−j 2π f τᵢ)  =  H_static(f) + H_dynamic(f, t)&#10;Each path rotates by a different angle at each f, so paths add up differently per subcarrier (frequency-selective fading). Motion changes only H_dynamic: amplitude and phase fluctuate (CARM, Wang et al. 2015)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=12;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="514" width="620" height="110" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="csi_panel" value="CSI: one complex value per subcarrier per antenna pair, every frame" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="680" y="62" width="570" height="300" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="csi_cap" value="Bars = |H| per subcarrier (schematic shape, no data). Grey = frame before, red dashed = frame after the person moved: the fingerprint changes shape. Subcarriers 312.5 kHz apart [1]; 52 used at 20 MHz legacy [2], 56 in 802.11n HT20 [3]; a 2x2 link has 4 antenna pairs [4], each with its own row." style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#ffffff;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="690" y="300" width="550" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="rssi_panel" value="RSSI: one power number per frame" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="680" y="376" width="570" height="126" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="rssi_a" value="frame before:&#10;one number" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="700" y="410" width="160" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="rssi_b" value="frame after:&#10;nearly the same" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;dashed=1;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="880" y="410" width="160" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="rssi_cap" value="Power summed over the whole channel. Two different motions can give the same RSSI change and different CSI changes [A1]." style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#ffffff;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1050" y="400" width="195" height="98" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="timing" value="How fast it fluctuates [A1]: one cycle per wavelength of path change; wavelength 12.3 cm at 2.4 GHz [5], 5.5 cm at 5 GHz [6]. A reflected path changes at up to 2x body speed, so a 1 m/s walk gives up to ~36 Hz at 5 GHz [7] (Doppler).&#10;CAUTION: beacon-driven CSI at an illustrative 10 Hz [8] cannot represent anything above 5 Hz (Nyquist, my arithmetic): you see aliased energy, not a clean Doppler spectrum." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="680" y="514" width="570" height="110" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="legend" value="Legend:  blue = radios | red, red dashed = dynamic (motion-dependent) | grey = static | purple = model | green frame = CSI (PHY-layer detail) | amber = RSSI and timing caveat.&#10;[A1], [A2] = kit notes. [n] = constants.json entry listed below; ILLUSTRATIVE values are round teaching values, never measurements." style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="636" width="1220" height="46" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="bb0" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#cccccc;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="712" y="217" width="26" height="75" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="ba0" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;dashed=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="718" y="204" width="26" height="87" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="bb1" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#cccccc;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="752" y="173" width="26" height="118" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="ba1" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;dashed=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="758" y="192" width="26" height="100" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="bb2" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#cccccc;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="792" y="129" width="26" height="162" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="ba2" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;dashed=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="798" y="167" width="26" height="125" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="bb3" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#cccccc;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="832" y="160" width="26" height="131" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="ba3" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;dashed=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="838" y="135" width="26" height="156" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="bb4" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#cccccc;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="872" y="223" width="26" height="68" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="ba4" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;dashed=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="878" y="185" width="26" height="106" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="bb5" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#cccccc;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="912" y="254" width="26" height="37" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="ba5" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;dashed=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="918" y="242" width="26" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="bb6" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#cccccc;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="952" y="232" width="26" height="60" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="ba6" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;dashed=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="958" y="254" width="26" height="37" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="bb7" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#cccccc;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="992" y="167" width="26" height="125" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="ba7" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;dashed=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="998" y="204" width="26" height="87" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="bb8" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#cccccc;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1032" y="104" width="26" height="187" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="ba8" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;dashed=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1038" y="142" width="26" height="150" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="bb9" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#cccccc;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1072" y="92" width="26" height="200" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="ba9" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;dashed=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1078" y="85" width="26" height="206" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="bb10" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#cccccc;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1112" y="148" width="26" height="143" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="ba10" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;dashed=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1118" y="117" width="26" height="175" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="bb11" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#cccccc;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1152" y="202" width="26" height="90" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="ba11" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;dashed=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1158" y="173" width="26" height="118" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="bb12" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#cccccc;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1192" y="242" width="26" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="ba12" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;dashed=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1198" y="223" width="26" height="68" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="axis_lbl" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#333333;strokeColor=#333333;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="700" y="291" width="540" height="2" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="src" value="Numbers (all loaded from constants.json):&#10;[1] ofdm_subcarrier_spacing_11a_n_ac - public; IEEE 802.11 OFDM PHY (clauses 17/19/21): 20 MHz / 64-point FFT&#10;[2] used_subcarriers_legacy_20MHz - public; IEEE 802.11a/g OFDM PHY&#10;[3] used_subcarriers_ht_20MHz - public; IEEE 802.11n HT20&#10;[4] mimo_2x2_streams - public; my arithmetic: 2 TX x 2 RX antennas&#10;[5] wavelength_2g4 - public; my arithmetic: speed_of_light / 2.437 GHz (channel 6)&#10;[6] wavelength_5g - public; my arithmetic: speed_of_light / 5.5 GHz (mid 5 GHz band)&#10;[7] doppler_walk_example_5g - public; my arithmetic: reflected path length changes at up to 2 x 1 m/s for an illustrative 1 m/s walk; f = 2 / wavelength_5g&#10;[8] csi_rate_beacon_illustrative - ILLUSTRATIVE; round value for passive beacon-driven CSI; consistent with beacon_rate_default; internal I2/I7 report the same order&#10;Notes: [A1] CSI and multipath (OFDM, CSI vs RSSI, static/dynamic paths, Doppler, Nyquist caution); [A2] what the hardware gives you. Public refs: IEEE 802.11 OFDM PHY; Ma, Zhou, Wang, CSUR 2019; Wang et al. MobiCom 2015 (CARM); Qian et al. 2017 (Widar/WiDance Doppler)." style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=9;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="694" width="1220" height="132" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="line0" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;strokeColor=#666666;strokeWidth=2;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="170" y="281" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="500" y="281" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="line1" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#666666;strokeWidth=1.5;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="130" y="250" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="330" y="112" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="line2" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;strokeColor=#666666;strokeWidth=1.5;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="330" y="112" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="545" y="250" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="line3" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=2;dashed=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="150" y="312" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="300" y="432" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="line4" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=2;dashed=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="356" y="432" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="520" y="312" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram><diagram id="p_02_single_link_sensitivity" name="02-single-link-sensitivity"><mxGraphModel dx="800" dy="600" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1280" pageHeight="768" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="0" /><mxCell id="1" parent="0" /><mxCell id="title" value="One link sees motion best near its two radios, less mid-link, and almost nothing a few metres off the line of sight or behind a wall" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#ffffff;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="12" width="1240" height="34" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="scene" value="One link, seen from above (schematic: zone widths exaggerated, not to scale) [A1]" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fbfbfb;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="60" width="860" height="470" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="band" value="walking visible out to about 4 m from the LoS [1] (illustrative); hand-waving about 3 m [2]" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;dashed=1;fillColor=#f3f7fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#6c8ebf;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="110" width="800" height="330" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="z3" value="" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#bbbbbb;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="75" y="190" width="740" height="200" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="z2" value="" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="95" y="222" width="700" height="136" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="z1" value="" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#ece4f1;strokeColor=#9673a6;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="115" y="254" width="660" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="z3l" value="zone 3" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#777777;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="415" y="192" width="60" height="26" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="z2l" value="zone 2" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#555555;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="415" y="224" width="60" height="26" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="z1l" value="first Fresnel zone" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#9673a6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="385" y="256" width="120" height="22" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="tx" value="AP&#10;(transmitter)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="56" y="264" width="96" height="52" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="rx" value="device&#10;(receiver)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="738" y="264" width="96" height="52" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="pA" value="A" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="168" y="296" width="34" height="34" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="pB" value="B" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="428" y="292" width="34" height="34" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="pC" value="C" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#eeeeee;strokeColor=#666666;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="600" y="390" width="34" height="34" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="wall" value="wall" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=9;fillColor=#bbbbbb;strokeColor=#666666;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="452" width="800" height="14" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="pD" value="D" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;dashed=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#666666;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="430" y="478" width="34" height="34" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="pD_l" value="D: next room, behind the wall - most of the effect removed [A1]; but what remains is a through-wall false positive [B4]" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="470" y="476" width="380" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="pat" value="What one link sees - a power-fading simulation and single-link measurements agreed [A1]:&#10;&#10;A  motion close to EITHER radio changes the CSI most (red).&#10;&#10;B  on the LoS, motion mid-link changes it LESS than near the ends: the first zone is narrowest at the radios, so a body there fills more of it (amber).&#10;&#10;C  sensitivity falls steeply outside the first zone (grey).&#10;&#10;Also: motion ON the LoS drops power more than motion beside it." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#eeeeee;strokeColor=#666666;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="910" y="60" width="340" height="250" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="fz" value="Fresnel zones (Wang et al. UbiComp 2016): nested ellipses with the radios at the foci; zone n ends where a reflected path is n half-wavelengths longer than the LoS. First-zone radius at mid-link:&#10;      r1 = 0.5 x sqrt(lambda x d)&#10;For an illustrative d = 4 m link [3]:&#10;   0.23 m at 5 GHz, 0.35 m at 2.4 GHz [4]&#10;A body crossing zone boundaries makes one fluctuation per boundary." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="910" y="322" width="340" height="208" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="so" value="So what: placement decides coverage. A room with no device is covered only weakly, through walls, and one link cannot tell motion near its AP end from motion near its device end - only a comparison across several links resolves that [B4, C5]." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="542" width="1220" height="52" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="legend" value="Legend: blue = radios | purple fill = first Fresnel zone, grey rings = zones 2-3 | dashed blue = illustrative detectable band | target fill: red = large change, amber = smaller, grey = weak, dashed white = behind a wall.  [A1], [B4], [C5] = kit notes; [n] = constants.json entries below." style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="604" width="1220" height="44" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="src" value="Numbers (all loaded from constants.json):&#10;[1] single_link_range_illustrative - ILLUSTRATIVE; illustrative distance beyond which walking motion is hard to see on one link; internal I1 reports the same order&#10;[2] small_motion_range_illustrative - ILLUSTRATIVE; illustrative range for hand-waving detection; internal I1&#10;[3] link_length_illustrative - ILLUSTRATIVE; round room-scale link length used for the Fresnel example in A1&#10;[4] fresnel_first_zone_mid_radius_example - public; my arithmetic: r1 = 0.5 x sqrt(lambda x d) at the midpoint of a link of illustrative length d = 4 m (link_length_illustrative); formula from Fresnel-zone model, Wang et al. UbiComp 2016&#10;Notes: [A1] CSI and multipath (Fresnel zones, single-link patterns, range, wall); [B4] multi-device joint detection; [C5] limits. Public ref: Wang et al., UbiComp 2016 (Fresnel-zone model)." style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=9;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="658" width="1220" height="96" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="line0" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;strokeColor=#444444;strokeWidth=2;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="152" y="290" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="738" y="290" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram><diagram id="p_03_processing_chain" name="03-processing-chain"><mxGraphModel dx="800" dy="600" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1280" pageHeight="902" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="0" /><mxCell id="1" parent="0" /><mxCell id="title" value="The signal chain moved the result more than the model did: cheap preprocessing, features whose scale does not depend on the room, then any small classifier" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#ffffff;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="12" width="1240" height="34" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="row1_lbl" value="PREPROCESSING [B1] - every step is a median, a norm or a moving average" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#6c8ebf;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="31" y="54" width="900" height="20" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="raw" value="Raw CSI report&#10;one frame: |H| per&#10;subcarrier, with a&#10;real timestamp [A2]" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#eeeeee;strokeColor=#666666;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="78" width="124" height="96" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="s1" value="1  Power-normalise&#10;divide by L2 norm&#10;(removes AGC gain&#10;jumps)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="166" y="78" width="124" height="96" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="s2" value="2  Drop bad&#10;subcarriers&#10;guard-adjacent,&#10;very low amplitude" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="302" y="78" width="124" height="96" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="s3" value="3  Background&#10;moving average per&#10;subcarrier = static&#10;channel" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="438" y="78" width="124" height="96" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="s4" value="4  Dynamics&#10;amplitude minus&#10;background = the&#10;motion part [A1]" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="574" y="78" width="124" height="96" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="s5" value="5  Energy series&#10;L2 norm of the&#10;dynamics: one&#10;number per report" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="710" y="78" width="124" height="96" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="s6" value="6  Hampel filter&#10;flag if &gt; 3 x 1.4826 MAD&#10;from the median of&#10;+/-10 reports [1][2][3]" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="846" y="78" width="124" height="96" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="s7" value="7  Replace&#10;flagged reports&#10;with the window&#10;median" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="982" y="78" width="124" height="96" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="s8" value="8  Smooth&#10;(optional)&#10;exponential&#10;moving average" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1118" y="78" width="124" height="96" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="row2_lbl" value="FEATURES [B2] and CLASSIFIER [B3] - one window on one link at a time" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#82b366;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="150" y="210" width="900" height="20" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="win" value="Window&#10;K subcarriers x L reports&#10;on one link&#10;&#10;illustrative 1 s or 4 s [4][5]" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#eeeeee;strokeColor=#666666;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="240" width="190" height="150" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="f_acf" value="ACF (lag 1, averaged over subcarriers): ~1 when still, falls toward 0 with motion; lies in [-1, 1] in every room" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="270" y="240" width="330" height="46" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="f_pca" value="PCA eigenvalues of the K x K covariance: still = one dominant eigenvalue; motion spreads energy to the 2nd and later" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="270" y="292" width="330" height="46" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="f_fft" value="FFT per subcarrier, DC bin REMOVED (it encodes the room) and the top third of bins dropped as noise [6]" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="270" y="344" width="330" height="46" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="clf" value="Classifier ladder [B3]&#10;- threshold on one feature&#10;- SVM (RBF kernel)&#10;- small MLP on FFT features, illustrative 128 + 32 hidden units [7]&#10;- (sequence / CNN models: too little data)&#10;Score -&gt; threshold set by the false-alarm budget [C1]" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="650" y="240" width="300" height="150" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="out" value="Per-link, per-window motion probability&#10;&#10;-&gt; fused across all links of the home [B4]" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1000" y="240" width="250" height="150" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="c_grp" value="Group adjacent subcarriers (Ng = 4; 802.11 uses Ng in 1/2/4 [8]): NO loss, 4x less data. Adjacent subcarriers are strongly correlated [B1]." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="406" width="295" height="66" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="c_sel" value="Keep only the top 10% of subcarriers [9] by mean amplitude: about 4 TPR points lost, about 90% of feature compute saved [10] (illustrative)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="338" y="406" width="295" height="66" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="c_res" value="DO NOT resample to a uniform time grid: interpolation manufactured smooth samples where reports were missing and clearly hurt detection. Use real timestamps [B1, A2]." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="646" y="406" width="295" height="66" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="c_ph" value="Phase: random offsets per report. Sanitise only with 2+ receive antennas (linear fit, conjugate product, CSI ratio). A single-stream link uses amplitude only [A2, B1]." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="954" y="406" width="296" height="66" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="ev1" value="What the studies showed (ILLUSTRATIVE values, direction is the lesson):&#10;- preprocessing raised average TPR by about 10 points, and by about 30 points in the hardest scenarios (room with no device, small motion, near the AP) [11]&#10;- single link, TPR at 1% FPR: variance 0.4, ACF lag 1 0.65 [12]; FFT + small net 0.6 [13]" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="484" width="610" height="84" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="ev2" value="How the result must be tested (ILLUSTRATIVE):&#10;- same features and classifier: 0.9 accuracy on a random split, 0.6 on an unseen day [14][15] - split by time and by home, never at random [B3]&#10;- leave-one-home-out: best home 0.95 TPR, worst home 0.05 [16] - the home is the unit of generalisation" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="654" y="484" width="596" height="84" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="legend" value="Legend: grey = input / window | blue = preprocessing step (red-outlined cards = traps) | green = room-independent feature, green panel = evidence | purple = classifier | amber = output | red panel = evaluation trap.  [A1]-[C1] = kit notes; [n] = constants.json entries below." style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="580" width="1220" height="44" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="src" value="Numbers (all loaded from constants.json):&#10;[1] hampel_threshold_typical - public; conventional Hampel threshold (Pearson 2002; MATLAB hampel default)&#10;[2] hampel_mad_scale - public; Hampel filter / MAD consistency constant for Gaussian data (Pearson, IEEE Trans. Control Syst. Technol. 2002)&#10;[3] hampel_halfwidth_illustrative - ILLUSTRATIVE; illustrative Hampel neighbourhood; internal I7&#10;[4] window_short_illustrative - ILLUSTRATIVE; round analysis window used in early single-link work; internal I1/I2&#10;[5] window_long_illustrative - ILLUSTRATIVE; round analysis window used in later feature studies; internal I7&#10;[6] fft_high_freq_drop_illustrative - ILLUSTRATIVE; illustrative: the top third of frequency bins was discarded as noise-dominated; internal I7&#10;[7] mlp_hidden_units_illustrative - ILLUSTRATIVE; illustrative small MLP on concatenated FFT features; internal I7&#10;[8] beamforming_grouping_ng - public; IEEE 802.11n/ac compressed beamforming feedback, grouping parameter Ng&#10;[9] subcarrier_keep_fraction_illustrative - ILLUSTRATIVE; illustrative 'top 10%' selection; internal I7&#10;[10] subcarrier_selection_cost_illustrative - ILLUSTRATIVE; illustrative relation: keeping 10% of subcarriers costs a few TPR points and saves about 90% of feature compute; internal I7&#10;[11] preprocessing_gain_illustrative - ILLUSTRATIVE; illustrative order of the event-level gain from the preprocessing chain, average vs hardest scenario; internal I7&#10;[12] acf_vs_variance_illustrative - ILLUSTRATIVE; illustrative gap between a self-normalised ACF feature and raw variance; internal I7&#10;[13] single_feature_tpr_illustrative - ILLUSTRATIVE; illustrative ordering of single-link features; internal I7 feature comparison&#10;[14] split_random_accuracy_illustrative - ILLUSTRATIVE; illustrative accuracy on a random train/test split of the same days; internal I2&#10;[15] split_heldout_day_accuracy_illustrative - ILLUSTRATIVE; illustrative accuracy when testing on an unseen day; internal I2&#10;[16] home_spread_illustrative - ILLUSTRATIVE; illustrative spread for a simple ACF+variance+SVM detector in leave-one-home-out tests; internal I7&#10;Notes: [A1] multipath; [A2] hardware; [B1] preprocessing; [B2] features; [B3] classifiers and windows; [B4] joint detection; [C1] KPIs. Public refs: Hampel 1974, Pearson 2002 (Hampel/MAD); Zhang et al. 2018-2019 (ACF); Wang et al. 2015 (CARM, PCA); Kotaru et al. 2015, Li et al. 2017, Zeng et al. 2019 (phase); Cortes and Vapnik 1995 (SVM)." style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=9;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="636" width="1220" height="250" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="line0" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#666666;strokeWidth=1.5;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="1180" y="174" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="1180" y="200" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="line1" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#666666;strokeWidth=1.5;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="1180" y="200" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="125" y="200" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="line2" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;strokeColor=#666666;strokeWidth=1.5;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="125" y="200" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="125" y="238" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge0" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontColor=#6c8ebf;" edge="1" parent="1" source="raw" target="s1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge1" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontColor=#6c8ebf;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s1" target="s2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge2" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontColor=#6c8ebf;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s2" target="s3"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge3" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontColor=#6c8ebf;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s3" target="s4"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge4" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontColor=#6c8ebf;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s4" target="s5"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge5" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontColor=#6c8ebf;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s5" target="s6"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge6" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontColor=#6c8ebf;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s6" target="s7"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge7" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontColor=#6c8ebf;" edge="1" parent="1" source="s7" target="s8"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge8" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;strokeColor=#82b366;fontColor=#82b366;" edge="1" parent="1" source="win" target="f_acf"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge9" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;strokeColor=#82b366;fontColor=#82b366;" edge="1" parent="1" source="win" target="f_pca"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge10" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;strokeColor=#82b366;fontColor=#82b366;" edge="1" parent="1" source="win" target="f_fft"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge11" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.3;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontColor=#9673a6;" edge="1" parent="1" source="f_acf" target="clf"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge12" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontColor=#9673a6;" edge="1" parent="1" source="f_pca" target="clf"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge13" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontColor=#9673a6;" edge="1" parent="1" source="f_fft" target="clf"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge14" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;strokeColor=#d79b00;fontColor=#d79b00;" edge="1" parent="1" source="clf" target="out"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram><diagram id="p_04_joint_detection" name="04-joint-detection"><mxGraphModel dx="800" dy="600" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1280" pageHeight="814" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="0" /><mxCell id="1" parent="0" /><mxCell id="uline0" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=2.2;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="196.84" y="109.46075949367089" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="125.16" y="111.72911392405064" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="uline1" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=2.2;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="291.12" y="121.72171875" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="456.88" y="168.98921875" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="uline2" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=2.2;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="230.05671826625388" y="134.46" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="96.47578947368422" y="407.54" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="uline3" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=2.2;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="263.9713931888545" y="134.46" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="480.4063157894737" y="407.54" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="uline4" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.6;dashed=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="130.28" y="120.43729468599034" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="453.72" y="173.56270531400966" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="uline5" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.6;dashed=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="85.0" y="136.36" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="85.0" y="407.64" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="uline6" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.6;dashed=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="115.41207547169812" y="136.36" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="468.58792452830187" y="407.64" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="uline7" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.6;dashed=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="462.568" y="203.0" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="121.432" y="409.0" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="uline8" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.6;dashed=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="499.0" y="203.0" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="499.0" y="409.0" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="uline9" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.6;dashed=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="130.28" y="431.0" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="453.72" y="431.0" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="title" value="One link cannot tell AP-side from device-side motion; compare links across devices - and add device-to-device links, because links grow as N x N" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#ffffff;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="12" width="1240" height="34" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="home_lbl" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="50" width="530" height="10" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="room1" value="room 1" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#888888;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="64" width="262" height="200" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="room2" value="room 2" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#888888;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="300" y="64" width="262" height="200" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="room3" value="room 3" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#888888;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="272" width="262" height="200" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="room4" value="room 4" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#888888;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="300" y="272" width="262" height="200" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="ap" value="AP" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="200" y="88" width="86" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="d1" value="device 1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="48" y="96" width="74" height="34" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="d2" value="device 2" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="462" y="164" width="74" height="34" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="d3" value="device 3" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="48" y="414" width="74" height="34" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="d4" value="device 4" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="462" y="414" width="74" height="34" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="pa" value="P" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=9;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="222" y="140" width="26" height="26" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="pa_l" value="motion near the AP:&#10;all AP links move together" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=9;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#ffffff;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#b85450;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="150" y="170" width="150" height="34" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="pb" value="Q" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=9;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="430" y="440" width="26" height="26" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="pb_l" value="motion near device 4:&#10;only its links move" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=right;fontSize=9;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#ffffff;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#b85450;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="306" y="432" width="120" height="34" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="links" value="Link graph [B4]: blue solid = AP-device links (N); green dashed = device-to-device links via a softAP on each device, same channel as the AP, MAC-filtered. With N = 4 devices [1]: 4 AP links become 16 directed links (N x N, my arithmetic) - and the new links cross rooms the AP links never cross." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#666666;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="482" width="532" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="wall" value="Through-wall false positives: motion next door reaches the links through the wall, weakened. Mitigate with more endpoints (the right room responds much more strongly), per-home sensitivity for thin walls, and fusion with a sensor that does not see through walls [B4]." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="564" width="532" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="rule_h" value="Decision rule: cross-correlate CSI variation across devices [B4]" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="590" y="64" width="660" height="26" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="r1" value="HIGH correlation across all AP links  -&gt;  motion near the AP (P): every AP link shares the AP end" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="590" y="94" width="660" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="r2" value="LOW correlation, one device's links active  -&gt;  motion near that device (Q)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="590" y="140" width="660" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="r3" value="Several devices active, LOW mutual correlation  -&gt;  several people, each near a device" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="590" y="186" width="660" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="sn" value="Where: sorted nodes and sorted links [B4]. Node variation w_i = sum_j v_ij; the node with the largest w is probably closest. Take links in order of v; if one end's w is clearly larger (w_i &gt; w_j + T, margin T found empirically), keep the half-plane on that side of the link's perpendicular bisector. The intersection of kept half-planes is the detected area; often the first two or three links decide the room. Equal w at three nodes -&gt; answer &quot;near several nodes&quot;. Needs rough device positions." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#666666;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="590" y="238" width="660" height="118" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="ch_h" value="Home-level TPR at 1% FPR (ILLUSTRATIVE) [2]" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="590" y="366" width="660" height="24" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="bar0" value="0.5" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#eeeeee;strokeColor=#666666;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="690" y="505" width="90" height="95" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="bl0" value="1 device&#10;AP link only&#10;1 link" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="678" y="604" width="114" height="46" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="bar1" value="0.75" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="806" y="458" width="90" height="142" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="bl1" value="4 devices&#10;AP links only&#10;4 links" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="794" y="604" width="114" height="46" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="bar2" value="0.95" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="922" y="420" width="90" height="180" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="bl2" value="4 devices&#10;AP + device-to-device&#10;16 links" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="910" y="604" width="114" height="46" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="tick0" value="0" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=right;fontSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="630" y="591" width="40" height="18" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="tick5" value="0.5" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=right;fontSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="630" y="496" width="40" height="18" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="tick10" value="1" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=right;fontSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="630" y="401" width="40" height="18" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="ch_note" value="Same four devices: adding device-to-device links gained more than going from one device to four on AP links. By scenario [3]: near a device 0.95, room with no device 0.6, typing 0.4." style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#ffffff;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1040" y="420" width="210" height="150" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="legend" value="Legend: blue = AP and AP-device links | green = devices, device-to-device links (dashed) | red P, Q = example motions | amber = through-wall caveat | bars: grey 1 device, blue 4 devices AP links, green 4 devices all links.  [B4] = kit note; [n] = constants.json entries below." style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="662" width="1220" height="44" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="src" value="Numbers (all loaded from constants.json):&#10;[1] home_study_size_illustrative - ILLUSTRATIVE; illustrative shape of a cross-home study; internal I7&#10;[2] devices_tpr_illustrative - ILLUSTRATIVE; illustrative relation: more endpoints help, device-to-device links help more; internal I7&#10;[3] motion_type_tpr_illustrative - ILLUSTRATIVE; illustrative per-scenario spread; internal I7&#10;Notes: [B4] multi-device joint detection (softAP links, cross-correlation rule, sorted nodes/links, through-wall false positives, device-count result); see also [C5] one-device homes. hostapd is open-source." style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=9;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="716" width="1220" height="84" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="line0" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#333333;strokeWidth=1.5;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="672" y="600" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="1030" y="600" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="line1" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#333333;strokeWidth=1.5;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="672" y="600" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="672" y="410" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="line2" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#bbbbbb;strokeWidth=1;dashed=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="672" y="410" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="1022" y="410" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram><diagram id="p_05_room_metric_learning" name="05-room-metric-learning"><mxGraphModel dx="800" dy="600" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1280" pageHeight="648" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="0" /><mxCell id="1" parent="0" /><mxCell id="title" value="Room localisation by metric learning: learn &quot;same room vs different room&quot; once from many homes - then a new home needs one calibration walk, not a new model" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#ffffff;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="12" width="1240" height="34" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="h1" value="1  TRAIN once, on many homes [B5]" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="58" width="390" height="30" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="h2" value="2  CALIBRATE once per new home [B5]" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="445" y="58" width="390" height="30" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="h3" value="3  INFER: nearest reference embedding [B5]" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="860" y="58" width="390" height="30" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="t_data" value="CSI windows (subcarriers x time) from many homes, each labelled with the room the person was in (link labelling rule [B3])" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#eeeeee;strokeColor=#666666;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="100" width="390" height="54" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="t_a" value="anchor&#10;room K, home H" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#9673a6;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="172" width="118" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="t_p" value="positive&#10;same room K" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="166" y="172" width="118" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="t_n" value="negative&#10;other room, SAME home" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="302" y="172" width="118" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="t_net" value="ONE shared network (Siamese) embeds all three. Options: 1-D conv over time + weighting over subcarriers; 1-D conv over time then over subcarriers; or 2-D conv on the window as an image." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="242" width="390" height="70" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="t_loss" value="Triplet loss: require  d(anchor, negative) &gt; d(anchor, positive) + margin.&#10;FaceNet uses a margin of 0.2 on unit-length embeddings [1] (public).&#10;Contrastive loss (pairs) is the alternative: pull same-room pairs together, push other-room pairs a margin apart." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#9673a6;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="330" width="390" height="96" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="c_walk" value="The user walks through each room once while the devices record CSI (the calibration walk)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="445" y="100" width="390" height="54" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="c_emb" value="Embed those windows with the trained network (no retraining)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="445" y="172" width="390" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="c_ref" value="Store one or a few REFERENCE embeddings per room of THIS home. Any number of rooms, any layout." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="445" y="242" width="390" height="70" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="c_age" value="References age: furniture, doors and device moves change the CSI, so the walk must be refreshed [B5, C5]. Metric learning removes labels in the deployed home - it does NOT remove the need for many training homes." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="445" y="330" width="390" height="96" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="space" value="Embedding space of one home (schematic, 2-D for drawing)" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#fbfbfb;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="860" y="100" width="390" height="326" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="kA" value="kitchen" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;dashed=1;fillColor=#e8f0fa;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="890" y="150" width="120" height="84" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="kB" value="living room" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;dashed=1;fillColor=#ecf5e8;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1070" y="140" width="130" height="90" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="kC" value="bedroom" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=bottom;align=center;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;dashed=1;fillColor=#f4ecf7;strokeColor=#9673a6;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="950" y="290" width="130" height="84" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="rA" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#6c8ebf;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="942" y="186" width="14" height="14" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="rB" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#82b366;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1128" y="176" width="14" height="14" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="rC" value="" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#9673a6;strokeColor=#9673a6;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1008" y="318" width="14" height="14" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="live" value="" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;fillColor=#b85450;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1098" y="244" width="18" height="18" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="live_l" value="live window -&gt; nearest&#10;reference = living room" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#b85450;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1056" y="262" width="184" height="36" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="far" value="" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=11;dashed=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1190" y="330" width="18" height="18" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="far_l" value="farther than every reference&#10;-&gt; answer &quot;unknown&quot;: empty&#10;or the home has changed" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=right;fontSize=10;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#b85450;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1096" y="350" width="150" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="why" value="Why not a room classifier [B5]: a classifier has one output per class. A model trained on four-room homes has no meaning in a six-room home, and retraining per home needs a large labelled dataset. Metric learning turns per-home CLASSIFICATION (does not scale) into per-home CALIBRATION (one walk)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="444" width="600" height="66" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="also" value="Two side uses [B5]: (1) single-device tests can still TRAIN on device-to-device links labelled by the room rule, adding data without changing what is available at test time; (2) devices whose CSI changes look alike are probably in the same room - auto-assign smart-home devices to rooms." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#eeeeee;strokeColor=#666666;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="650" y="444" width="600" height="66" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="legend" value="Legend: purple = training (one network for all homes) | blue = per-home calibration | green = inference; dashed ellipses = rooms, squares = reference embeddings, red dot = live window, hollow red = unknown | amber = drift caveat | red panel = the reason for the design.  [B3], [B5], [C5] = kit notes." style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="522" width="1220" height="44" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="src" value="Numbers (all loaded from constants.json):&#10;[1] triplet_margin_facenet - public; Schroff, Kalenichenko, Philbin, 'FaceNet', CVPR 2015, alpha&#10;Notes: [B5] room localisation by metric learning (no result numbers - a proposed method); [B3] link labelling; [C5] drift. Public refs: Hadsell, Chopra, LeCun, CVPR 2006 (contrastive); Schroff, Kalenichenko, Philbin, CVPR 2015 (FaceNet, triplet)." style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=9;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="578" width="1220" height="56" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="line0" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.8;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="1107" y="244" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="1136" y="192" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="edge0" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;exitX=0.15;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontColor=#9673a6;" edge="1" parent="1" source="t_data" target="t_a"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge1" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontColor=#9673a6;" edge="1" parent="1" source="t_data" target="t_p"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge2" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;exitX=0.85;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontColor=#9673a6;" edge="1" parent="1" source="t_data" target="t_n"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge3" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.15;entryY=0;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontColor=#9673a6;" edge="1" parent="1" source="t_a" target="t_net"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge4" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontColor=#9673a6;" edge="1" parent="1" source="t_p" target="t_net"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge5" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.85;entryY=0;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontColor=#9673a6;" edge="1" parent="1" source="t_n" target="t_net"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge6" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontColor=#9673a6;" edge="1" parent="1" source="t_net" target="t_loss"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge7" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontColor=#6c8ebf;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c_walk" target="c_emb"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge8" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontColor=#6c8ebf;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c_emb" target="c_ref"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge9" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;dashed=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.3;entryX=0;entryY=0.7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontColor=#9673a6;" edge="1" parent="1" source="t_net" target="c_emb"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge10" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;fontSize=10;dashed=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.65;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontColor=#6c8ebf;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c_ref" target="space"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram><diagram id="p_06_false_alarm_budget" name="06-false-alarm-budget"><mxGraphModel dx="800" dy="600" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1280" pageHeight="702" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="0" /><mxCell id="1" parent="0" /><mxCell id="uline0" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#e2e2e2;strokeWidth=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="145" y="112.0" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="620" y="112.0" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="uline1" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#e2e2e2;strokeWidth=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="145" y="168.0" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="620" y="168.0" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="uline2" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#e2e2e2;strokeWidth=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="145" y="224.0" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="620" y="224.0" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="uline3" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#e2e2e2;strokeWidth=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="145" y="280.0" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="620" y="280.0" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="uline4" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#e2e2e2;strokeWidth=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="145" y="336.0" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="620" y="336.0" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="uline5" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#e2e2e2;strokeWidth=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="145" y="392.0" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="620" y="392.0" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="uline6" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#e2e2e2;strokeWidth=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="145" y="448.0" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="620" y="448.0" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="title" value="&quot;1% FPR&quot; is about 26 000 false alarms per home per month - a budget of 4 needs a per-window FPR near 1.5 x 10⁻⁶: fix the budget first" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#ffffff;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="12" width="1240" height="34" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="chart" value="Per-window false-positive rate (log scale) and what it means at one decision per 1 s [1]" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="58" width="620" height="470" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="ax_l" value="left: per-window FPR | right of axis: false&#10;alarms per 30 days [2] (my arithmetic)" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#555555;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="36" y="470" width="240" height="36" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="tk1" value="10⁻¹" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=right;fontSize=10;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="86" y="103" width="58" height="18" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="tm1" value="259 200 / month" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#777777;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="156" y="114" width="90" height="16" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="tk2" value="10⁻²" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=right;fontSize=10;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="86" y="159" width="58" height="18" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="tm2" value="25 920 / month" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#777777;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="156" y="170" width="90" height="16" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="tk3" value="10⁻³" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=right;fontSize=10;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="86" y="215" width="58" height="18" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="tm3" value="2592 / month" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#777777;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="156" y="226" width="90" height="16" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="tk4" value="10⁻⁴" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=right;fontSize=10;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="86" y="271" width="58" height="18" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="tm4" value="259 / month" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#777777;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="156" y="282" width="90" height="16" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="tk5" value="10⁻⁵" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=right;fontSize=10;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="86" y="327" width="58" height="18" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="tm5" value="26 / month" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#777777;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="156" y="338" width="90" height="16" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="tk6" value="10⁻⁶" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=right;fontSize=10;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="86" y="383" width="58" height="18" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="tm6" value="3 / month" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#777777;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="156" y="394" width="90" height="16" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="tk7" value="10⁻⁷" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=right;fontSize=10;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="86" y="439" width="58" height="18" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="tm7" value="0.26 / month" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#777777;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="156" y="450" width="90" height="16" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="res" value="Research operating point: TPR at 1% FPR [B3]&#10;= about 26 000 false windows per month (my arithmetic)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="300" y="142" width="330" height="52" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="bud" value="Product budget: an illustrative 4 false alarms per home per month [3]&#10;-&gt; per-window FPR near 1.5 x 10⁻⁶ if every false window counts" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="300" y="355" width="330" height="52" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="gap" value="gap: about 3.8 orders of magnitude&#10;(3 to 4, my arithmetic)&#10;Partly closed by: merging touching false windows into one EVENT; requiring several positive windows in a row - both cost latency [C1]" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#b85450;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="330" y="208" width="290" height="96" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="lad_h" value="The KPI ladder: four stages, same six KPIs at each [C1]" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="670" y="58" width="580" height="24" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="col_home" value="home level" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="790" y="86" width="225" height="24" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="col_room" value="room level" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1025" y="86" width="225" height="24" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="row_m" value="motion&#10;(person moves)" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=right;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="670" y="114" width="110" height="70" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="row_p" value="presence&#10;(moving or still)" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=right;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="670" y="192" width="110" height="70" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="st1" value="1  motion anywhere in the home?&#10;hard part: non-human change" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="790" y="114" width="225" height="70" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="st2" value="2  which room has motion?&#10;hard part: adjacent rooms through walls" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1025" y="114" width="225" height="70" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="st3" value="3  anyone home, moving or still?&#10;hard part: a still person barely changes the CSI" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="790" y="192" width="225" height="70" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="st4" value="4  which room is a person in?&#10;hard part: both of the above" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1025" y="192" width="225" height="70" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="six" value="Six KPIs per stage: TPR, FPR, TNR, FNR (wrong room counts as a miss), BLIND-SPOT ratio (area or rooms where errors exceed a threshold), EFFECTIVE-COVERAGE ratio (area or rooms where TPR and TNR both pass). The last two turn an average into a map: a good average can still fail one room every day." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#666666;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="670" y="274" width="580" height="96" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="time" value="Time to detect (start of motion -&gt; first positive) and time to clear (exit -&gt; &quot;empty&quot;): report both as distributions with a high percentile, not a mean. State window-level vs event-level for every number." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#666666;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="670" y="380" width="580" height="66" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="fld" value="Why it matters (ILLUSTRATIVE): a lab demo looked near-perfect before false-positive cases were tested; the later field study at the product budget reached about 0.5 TPR against a target of 0.9 [4]. Causes: CSI outliers, drift over time, chip CSI quality [C1]." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=10;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="670" y="456" width="580" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="legend" value="Legend: red = research operating point / field shortfall | green = product budget, stage 1 | blue, amber, red stages = increasing difficulty | grey ticks = false alarms per 30 days at that FPR. Report every KPI per scenario (near a device, near the AP, door, far, room with no device, small motion, still, empty) [C1, C2]." style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="540" width="1220" height="44" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="src" value="Numbers (all loaded from constants.json):&#10;[1] window_short_illustrative - ILLUSTRATIVE; round analysis window used in early single-link work; internal I1/I2&#10;[2] seconds_per_30_days - public; arithmetic: 30 x 86400&#10;[3] false_alarm_budget_illustrative - ILLUSTRATIVE; illustrative product-level false-alarm budget; internal I7&#10;[4] field_tpr_vs_target_illustrative - ILLUSTRATIVE; illustrative field shortfall at a false-alarm budget of a few per month; internal I7&#10;Arithmetic (my arithmetic, as in [C1]): decisions per 30 days = seconds_per_30_days / window; false windows at 1% FPR = 0.01 x that; budget FPR = budget / decisions. Notes: [B3] TPR at fixed FPR; [C1] KPIs; [C2] scenario taxonomy. Public ref: Fawcett 2006 (ROC)." style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=9;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="596" width="1220" height="92" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="line0" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#333333;strokeWidth=1.5;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="150" y="112.0" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="150" y="448.0" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="line1" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=2.5;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="150" y="168.0" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="300" y="168.0" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="line2" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=0;strokeColor=#82b366;strokeWidth=2.5;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="150" y="381.4482003287532" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="300" y="381.4482003287532" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="line3" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=0;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=2;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="315" y="196.0" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="315" y="351.4482003287532" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>